1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,500
Dating apps ask who you like, then make you swipe and chat for days.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:18,000
DateDrop asks one smaller question: when are you free?

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:29,500
One free evening goes in. A real date comes out.

4
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Hard rules check age, mutual interest, distance, safety, budget, and real overlap.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:56,000
OpenAI ranks only the people who pass those rules. It cannot overrule one.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:09,500
Firecrawl researches real public venues on the live web around both people.

7
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:23,000
Every plan keeps its sources, evidence, timestamp, budget, and constraints.

8
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:37,000
AgentMail sends two separate invitations. Neither person sees the other's email.

9
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:50,000
I accept privately. The other person cannot see my answer yet.

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:03,000
A labelled demo persona lets a judge drive the second side.

11
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:16,500
Both accept. The untouched screen updates live through Convex—no refresh.

12
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:29,000
One acceptance reserves the evening. Two finalize the same calendar event.

13
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:40,000
A cancellation releases it instead of leaving a stale plan behind.

14
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:49,000
A trusted contact receives only my name, time, and the public venue.

15
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Afterward, each person can check in privately about outcome and safety.

16
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
We plan the date. You just say yes.
